            "body": "Implements extract(entries, root) using standard-library path inspection. It validates the list, entry types, POSIX names, duplicate and file/directory collisions, root, existing components, symlinks, and absent targets before creating anything. Files are created exclusively and receive the input bytes; unexpected I/O errors propagate. Added focused regression tests for invalid inputs, no-write preflight, target conflicts, symlink paths, exact bytes, and invalid roots. Verification: 13 unittest cases pass on the final head; diff check passes; compileall passed on the preceding implementation commit. Review scope: three whole-change reads from fe25cf18618399aa7901b8fbf70cd886591cc713 through bddfb2472f93fd4778c2cb74b7f5639529995e1f (two passes, one blocking finding); the root ancestor classification finding was fixed in 0a865ec9c5c8598601488efc1bcba25a0ff17172 and passed a delta review from bddfb2472f93fd4778c2cb74b7f5639529995e1f. No advisory findings remain. Assumes the caller keeps the filesystem stable; rollback after I/O errors is outside the documented API.",
